[h1]BusStop Economy Integration Guide[/h1]

This guide is intended for [b]bank mod authors[/b] who want their mod to natively support BusStop Fast Travel as a payment backend.

[hr]

[h2]How it works[/h2]

BusStop calls your mod through a Lua global API table that you expose. Your mod stays in full control of how balances are stored — BusStop never touches your internal data directly.

When a player travels, BusStop:
[list]
[*]Deducts available inventory items first (if [b]Pay with Items[/b] is enabled on the server)
[*]Calls your API's [b]canAfford[/b] with the [b]remaining amount[/b] (may be the full fare if items are disabled or insufficient)
[*]If affordable, calls [b]deduct[/b] for that remaining amount
[/list]

[hr]

[h2]Adding the API to your mod[/h2]

[h3]Where to put the code[/h3]

Create (or edit) a file inside your mod's server Lua folder:

[code]
mods/
└── MyBankMod/
    └── media/
        └── lua/
            └── server/
                └── MyBankMod_BusStopAPI.lua   ← new file (name is up to you)
[/code]

This file is loaded automatically by PZ on the server — no [b]require[/b], no [b]mod.info[/b] changes needed.

[h3]What to write[/h3]

In that file, expose a global table with an [b].API[/b] sub-table:

[code]
-- Inside your bank mod's server Lua file

MyBankMod = MyBankMod or {}

MyBankMod.API = {

    -- Returns true if the player can afford `amount`.
    -- amount = remaining fare after items were already deducted.
    -- On failure: false, errMsgKey, { label, needed, have }
    canAfford = function(player, amount)
        local balance = MyBankMod.getBalance(player)
        if balance >= amount then return true end
        return false, "err_no_currency", { "MyBank", tostring(amount), tostring(balance) }
    end,

    -- Deducts `amount`. Called only after canAfford returned true.
    deduct = function(player, amount)
        MyBankMod.setBalance(player, MyBankMod.getBalance(player) - amount)
    end,

    -- Returns a formatted price string shown in the travel UI.
    -- Only used when Pay with Items is disabled (bank-only mode).
    formatLabel = function(amount)
        if amount <= 0 then return "Free" end
        return "$" .. tostring(amount)
    end,
}
[/code]

That's all. No dependency on BusStop, no [b]require[/b], no events. If BusStop is not installed the table just sits unused.

[hr]

[h2]Server configuration[/h2]

Once your mod exposes the API, the server admin enables the integration via sandbox options:

[table]
[tr][th]Option[/th][th]Value[/th][/tr]
[tr][td]BusStop.UseBankPayment[/td][td]true[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]BusStop.BankModGlobal[/td][td]The exact name of your Lua global (e.g. MyBankMod)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td]BusStop.UseItemPayment[/td][td]true = items first, false = bank-only[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[b]Payment combinations:[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Items only[/b] (default) — UseItemPayment=true, UseBankPayment=false
[*][b]Bank only[/b] — UseItemPayment=false, UseBankPayment=true
[*][b]Items first, bank as overflow[/b] — UseItemPayment=true, UseBankPayment=true
[/list]

[hr]

[h2]Survivor Shop — bridge workaround[/h2]

Survivor Shop does not natively expose a [b].API[/b] table. If you are running a server with both mods and want them to work together [b]without modifying Survivor Shop's files[/b], you can create a small bridge script inside your server's [b]Lua/[/b] scripts folder (not inside either mod).

[i]Note: the ideal solution is for the Survivor Shop author to add the .API table directly to their mod.[/i]

[code]
-- File: <server>/Lua/SurvivorShopBusBridge.lua

SurvivorShopBus = SurvivorShopBus or {}

SurvivorShopBus.API = {

    canAfford = function(player, amount)
        if not SurvivorShop then
            return false, "err_no_currency", { "SS Bank", tostring(amount), "0" }
        end
        local key = SurvivorShop.getAccountKey(player)
        local md  = ModData.getOrCreate("SurvivorShop_Balances")
        local bal = (md.balances and tonumber(md.balances[key])) or 0
        if bal >= amount then return true end
        return false, "err_no_currency", { "SS Bank", tostring(amount), tostring(bal) }
    end,

    deduct = function(player, amount)
        if not SurvivorShop then return end
        local key = SurvivorShop.getAccountKey(player)
        local md  = ModData.getOrCreate("SurvivorShop_Balances")
        if not md.balances then md.balances = {} end
        local bal = tonumber(md.balances[key]) or 0
        md.balances[key] = math.max(0, bal - amount)
    end,

    formatLabel = function(amount)
        if amount <= 0 then return "Free" end
        return "$" .. string.format("%.2f", amount)
    end,
}
[/code]

Set [b]BusStop.BankModGlobal = SurvivorShopBus[/b] in sandbox options.

[hr]

[h2]Fail-safe behaviour[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Both options disabled[/b] — falls back to item-only, no crash
[*][b]BankModGlobal empty[/b] — travel blocked, error logged with [b][BusStop][ECON][/b] prefix
[*][b]Global not found[/b] — same (mod not loaded)
[*][b].API fields missing[/b] — same (integration incomplete)
[/list]

No crash, no silent money loss.

[hr]

[h2]Integration checklist (for mod authors)[/h2]

[list]
[*] Add [b]MyBankMod.API[/b] with [b]canAfford[/b], [b]deduct[/b], [b]formatLabel[/b] to a server-side Lua file in your mod
[*] Document the global name so server admins know what to set in [b]BankModGlobal[/b]
[*] Verify [b]canAfford[/b] handles amount = 0 gracefully (return true)
[*] Verify [b]deduct[/b] never sets balance below zero
[*] Test bank-only: UseItemPayment=false, UseBankPayment=true
[*] Test both active: have fewer items than the fare — items go first, bank covers the rest
[/list]
